# Tonal — Changelog

## v1.0.6 — Routing Reliability

- Routing configs are validated against live hardware before they are written; if any enabled channel's device is missing, nothing is written and the last good config stays in place
- Save & Apply re-detects hardware first, so ALSA card renumbering (after a reboot, reconnect or firmware update) no longer produces a config pointing at the wrong card
- Removed the PipeWire restart on every launch; Tonal now compares the on-disk config with the hardware present and asks for Save & Apply when it is out of date
- At login, PipeWire is restarted once only when the config is correct but devices enumerated late
- Routing rules for disabled or missing channels are skipped and logged instead of silently falling back to System
- Fixed toasts showing no text when the message contained "&"
- Fixed a VU meter thread crash when monitoring stopped mid-read
- Package files are now owned by root
- Added CLAUDE.md project guide; build artifacts are ignored by git

## v1.0.5 — In-App Updates and Hardware Detection

- In-app update check, download and install from GitHub Releases (Status page)
- Build script reads the version from constants.py and stamps the packaged copy; pre-flight compile and import checks before packaging
- Expanded output detected by capability (10-channel PCM) instead of card name or index
- Hotplug watch: USB port moves and (un)plugs are detected while Tonal is running
- Every generated PipeWire block is flagged nofail, so a missing device can't stop PipeWire from starting
- EQ band frequencies clamped to 20 Hz–20 kHz before reaching PipeWire
- Raw USB Chat and USB 2 outputs pinned to 100% on apply
- Status page lists the nodes Tonal actually generated

## v1.0.4 — Spectrum Analyzer

- Added real-time spectrum analyzer to the Equalizer page (GStreamer-based)
- 512-point FFT mapped to 31-band 1/3 octave display (ISO center frequencies)
- Peak hold markers with configurable hold time and decay
- Smooth bar animation with instant rise and gradual falloff
- Automatic start/stop lifecycle tied to application window
- Graceful degradation when GStreamer is unavailable
- Dark/light theme support matching existing VU meter style

## v1.0.3 — Version Display

- Added application version display to the Status page
- Version sourced from constants.py for single-source-of-truth consistency

## v1.0.2 — Phase 1 Refactor

- Centralized shared constants into constants.py (channel targets, file paths, filter types, sample rate)
- Extracted duplicated helpers into widgets/helpers.py (scrollable_wrap, block_scroll, load_themed_svg_icon, icon_button)
- Moved inline CSS from tonal.py to data/style.css
- Replaced magic strings with named constants across all modules
- Updated build script to include new files

## v1.0.1 — Bug Fixes

- Bug fixes and minor improvements

## v1.0.0 — Initial Release

- Multi-channel PipeWire routing for RODECaster Pro II (Expanded/Standard/USB 2)
- Parametric EQ with unlimited bands and 8 filter types
- Profile management (save, switch, delete, auto-backup)
- Import from EasyEffects JSON and Peace profiles
- Export to EqualizerAPO and EasyEffects formats
- Per-application audio routing rules with app discovery
- Real-time VU meter with peak hold and EQ peak overlay
- Live EQ updates without PipeWire restart
- Hardware auto-detection (USB 1 Expanded/Standard, USB 2)
- Zero Python package dependencies
- .deb package with desktop integration
